WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.720
- It's time for Moss or Ross.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.420
- [Ross] Oh.
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.350
(audience applauds)

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.440
- Okay, here's how it's gonna work.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.560
We're gonna pick a random fact

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.950
and we're gonna pop it up on the screen.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.090
And I have to decide who it pertains to.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.810
I'd love for you to play along, everybody.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.730
And since "Shining Girls"
is going to leave you

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:18.320
on the edge of your seat,

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.020
if I get the majority of them correct,

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.150
our audience is gonna go
home with this amazing prize

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.000
to help you relax.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.980
'Cause, boy, do we all need
to relax in this world.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.760
There's an intelligent
therapeutic massage device

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.020
from the company Lyric.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:33.430
So I would like to, you know,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.090
help you all relax.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.594
- Yeah. Yes.
(audience applauds)

00:00:37.594 --> 00:00:38.490
But Drew.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.087
- Um, all right.
- Drew, only though,

00:00:41.087 --> 00:00:43.070
I'm gonna say, but they only get it

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.680
if you're good at this game, right?

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.800
- Oh, God.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:46.930
Well, let me try.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:47.960
All right, number one.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.010
Let's see the first fact.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:53.800
Okay, fact one is "I once got third place

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.847
in a demolition derby."

00:00:56.711 --> 00:00:59.260
(audience laughs)
(Drew laughs)

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.800
- So we have to keep a
straight face, Elizabeth.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:02.633
- Yes.
- Which is,

00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:04.690
it's tough for me to
keep a straight anything,

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:05.823
so let me try.
- What do you guys think?

00:01:05.823 --> 00:01:08.164
(audience laughing)

00:01:08.164 --> 00:01:09.050
- [Audience Members] Ross.
- Ross.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.830
I feel like it might be Ross,

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.060
because of how and where you grew up.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.763
I'm gonna go with Ross.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:18.613
(bell pings)
- Yes.

00:01:18.613 --> 00:01:22.423
It is me.
(audience applauds)

00:01:22.423 --> 00:01:24.180
- Nice.
- Yes it is.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.013
- Nice.

00:01:25.013 --> 00:01:27.624
You're gonna need like five
of those massage tools.

00:01:27.624 --> 00:01:28.994
(Drew laughs and flusters)

00:01:28.994 --> 00:01:31.976
- Okay, Let's see what's
next, I'm so excited, okay.

00:01:31.976 --> 00:01:35.397
"I once appeared on the
screen with Hulk Hogan."

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.727
I'm going Moss for this one.

00:01:39.727 --> 00:01:41.918
- [Audience Members] Yeah.
- Moss.

00:01:41.918 --> 00:01:43.446
(bell pings)
(Drew squeals excitedly)

00:01:43.446 --> 00:01:46.673
(audience applauds)
- Oh wait, we have a clip.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.506
Let's take a look.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:48.886
- Oh, we have a clip.
- Oh, yeah.

00:01:48.886 --> 00:01:49.803
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:52.471
Look at that.
- Bad kitty!

00:01:52.471 --> 00:01:55.499
(cat meows)
(girl screams)

00:01:55.499 --> 00:01:57.356
(audience laughs)
- Uh-oh.

00:01:57.356 --> 00:01:58.292
- [Elizabeth] Look at that.

00:01:58.292 --> 00:02:01.110
(girl screams)

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:01.980
- Thanks.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.600
- Probably seven or eight.
- Get a goldfish.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.011
(audience applauds)

00:02:07.011 --> 00:02:08.384
- Wow!

00:02:08.384 --> 00:02:09.567
- Thank you.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.500
Thank you very much.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:12.820
- That was the most...

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.181
That's a whole suitcase
to unpack, in itself.

00:02:15.181 --> 00:02:16.187
- We all have to start somewhere, Drew.

00:02:16.187 --> 00:02:17.790
- I love that!
- Yeah, some of us

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:18.870
start with Steven Spielberg,

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.250
but some of us (laughs)
(Drew laughs)

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.690
yet some of us start with Hulk.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:22.801
- [Ross] Yeah. (giggles)

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.141
- I love Hulk Hogan.

00:02:24.141 --> 00:02:25.600
(Ross and Elizabeth laugh)

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.627
All right, next, fact three.

00:02:27.627 --> 00:02:32.627
"I've been alone to Disneyland
because I love it so much."

00:02:34.681 --> 00:02:35.660
- [Audience Members] Ross.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.206
- Oh, I love that
everybody is like, "Ross".

00:02:39.206 --> 00:02:41.000
- [Audience Members] Ross.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.200
- [Drew] Oh gosh.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.190
- Look at that innocent blinking.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.023
- You know what's so weird is

00:02:45.023 --> 00:02:49.170
my instinct is that it's Moss, but...

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.989
Oh God, I'm going against the grain now.

00:02:51.989 --> 00:02:53.410
- Hard.
(audience call out answers)

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:54.500
- All right, I'm going Moss.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.602
I'm going Moss.

00:02:55.602 --> 00:02:56.679
(bell pings)
(Drew squeals excitedly)

00:02:56.679 --> 00:02:59.930
- Yes!
(audience applauds)

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:00.763
By yourself?

00:03:01.626 --> 00:03:02.953
- (laughing) Yes.

00:03:02.953 --> 00:03:04.490
Yes, I grew up in LA,

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.130
and sometimes there wasn't anything to do.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.278
And I did, I drove to
Disneyland by myself.

00:03:09.278 --> 00:03:10.666
- [Ross] Aww, did you
get a churro, at least?

00:03:10.666 --> 00:03:12.100
- I had a great time, I
rode a couple of rides

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.180
and went home.
- Oh.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.860
- It was great.
- I love it.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.914
That's what it's there for.

00:03:16.914 --> 00:03:18.620
"The happiest place on Earth".
- Yeah.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.500
- We'll go with you next time, okay?

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.333
- Thank you.

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:22.750
I think I was excited I had a car

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.640
and I could drive somewhere and I wanted,

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.870
You know, I was like, "I
could drive anywhere I want.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:27.920
I'm gonna go to Disneyland."

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:28.753
- Yes.

00:03:28.753 --> 00:03:30.097
The world is your oyster.

00:03:30.097 --> 00:03:32.770
"Handmaid's Tale", Season
five explores freedom,

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.070
you go to Disneyland.
- (laughs) Exactly!

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.770
We all have our idea of freedom.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:37.777
- All right, number four.

00:03:37.777 --> 00:03:41.507
"I know how to install
a lighting fixture."

00:03:42.617 --> 00:03:44.119
(audience call out answers)

00:03:44.119 --> 00:03:45.387
Oh, oh.

00:03:45.387 --> 00:03:47.280
Oh, a little division here.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.113
I see.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.350
(audience call out answers)

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.521
I am gonna go Ross with this one.

00:03:52.521 --> 00:03:53.354
(bell pings)

00:03:53.354 --> 00:03:54.261
(Drew squeals)
- Yes.

00:03:54.261 --> 00:03:55.871
(audience applauds)
I'm very handy.

00:03:55.871 --> 00:03:57.270
- Very handy.
- I have a whole tool kit

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.440
and everything.
- Yes, you have.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.540
- I did a YouTube tutorial
and learned how to do it.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.650
- You're also like a walking pharmacy.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:04.770
You're very handy.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:06.890
Don't ever underestimate Ross.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.580
- No, I'm like MacGayver, all right.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.688
- Yes!
- I'll just solve any problem.

00:04:10.688 --> 00:04:11.896
(audience applauds)
- MacGayver.

00:04:11.896 --> 00:04:13.508
Yes.
- Done.

00:04:13.508 --> 00:04:14.670
- That is genius.

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:16.450
- Have you ever said that before?

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:17.930
- No, maybe one time.

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.670
- Well, that might have to be a thing.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.107
- Yeah, let's sell a whole sitcom.

00:04:21.107 --> 00:04:23.370
"MacGayver", here to solve the crime.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.810
All right, done. Sold.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.220
- Um, all right.
- You should copyright that.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.053
- We have one more.

00:04:27.053 --> 00:04:29.747
"My biggest fear is deep water."

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.819
I'm going Moss.

00:04:32.819 --> 00:04:33.844
(bell pings)
(Drew screams)

00:04:33.844 --> 00:04:35.712
- [Ross] Yes.
(audience applauds)

00:04:35.712 --> 00:04:36.662
That's it?

00:04:36.662 --> 00:04:38.628
Your fear?
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:38.628 --> 00:04:39.461
- Oh, that's a scary one.
- All right.

00:04:39.461 --> 00:04:41.500
I think I'm doing pretty good.
- Yes.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.210
- Did I get any wrong?

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:45.840
- No, you did not, Barrymore.
- No.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.139
You know you didn't.
(audience cheers)

00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:49.149
- [Ross] And you know what that means?

00:04:49.149 --> 00:04:50.698
- That means you're all going home

00:04:50.698 --> 00:04:55.698
with these dope, really cool,
amazing Lyric massage devices.

00:04:56.577 --> 00:04:59.697
I'm taking one and...
(audience applauds)

00:04:59.697 --> 00:05:01.557
Oh, Rossy, I love you so much.

00:05:01.557 --> 00:05:02.390
- I love you too.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.109
- Oh, Mossy, I love you so much.

00:05:04.109 --> 00:05:06.493
- I love you.
- Oh, God, I'm...

00:05:06.493 --> 00:05:08.827
This is such a dream come true for me.

00:05:08.827 --> 00:05:10.481
- For me too, are you kidding?

00:05:10.481 --> 00:05:11.730
It really, really is.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:13.840
- I have these giant pompoms

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.490
and they say, "Elizabeth Moss"
(Elizabeth chuckles)

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:17.820
and I'm always going like this.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:18.653
- Thank you.

00:05:18.653 --> 00:05:20.980
- Let it not be so long until
we see each other again.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.410
- I know, we can't do that.
- Life, travel,

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.050
work, pandemic.
- Let's not.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:24.883
- Please not.

00:05:24.883 --> 00:05:25.716
- Yes.
- Okay, good.

00:05:25.716 --> 00:05:26.890
You can catch Elizabeth

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.780
in the new series, "Shining Girls",

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.801
streaming now on Apple TV+.

00:05:30.801 --> 00:05:33.884
(bright theme music)

